BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 760 Td
14 TL
(FIREBASE SCHEMA FOR WEB APP) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This document defines a teammate-friendly Firebase Realtime Database schema for) Tj
T*
(the SmartGym web app.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The goal is simple:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- easy to understand in Firebase Console) Tj
T*
(- easy to explain to a frontend teammate) Tj
T*
(- still rich enough for session analysis) Tj
T*
(- preserves rep-level detail) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Product Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The web app should help staff, coaches, and athletes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- see which user trained on which day) Tj
T*
(- see what exercises they did) Tj
T*
(- track weekly and daily progress) Tj
T*
(- inspect machine-specific trends) Tj
T*
(- open one session and analyze sets and reps in detail) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Design Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(We keep sessions inside the week tree.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This is the best tradeoff for the current stage of the project because:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- it is easier to understand quickly) Tj
T*
(- all workouts for a user live under the correct week/day) Tj
T*
(- your teammate does not have to jump between summary and detail roots) Tj
T*
(- rep-level detail can still be preserved) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The important part is not splitting data into many roots. The important part is) Tj
T*
(organizing each session clearly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recommended Top-Level Nodes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use these roots:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `usersByRfid/{uid}`) Tj
T*
(- `calibrations/{uid}/{machineTypeId}`) Tj
T*
(- `calibrationHistory/{uid}/{machineTypeId}/{epoch}` optional) Tj
T*
(- `machineConfigs/{machineId}`) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
